Export a function `formatRelativeTime(date: Date, now?: Date): string` that
describes how long ago `date` was compared to `now` (default: the current time)
in English, using `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat` with `numeric: "auto"`.

Less than 45 seconds is "just now". Otherwise pick the largest fitting unit among
minutes, hours, days, weeks, months and years, e.g. "5 minutes ago", "yesterday",
"last week". Dates in the future work too ("in 3 hours").
